@startuml
title One chat turn: guidance, private facts, and streamed output
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 15
start
:POST /chat with thread_id + message;
if (Another reply for this user?) then (yes)
  :Return 409;
  stop
endif
:Load user-scoped chat checkpoint;
:Embed the question locally;
:Retrieve top 4 Chroma passages;
:Send source metadata to UI;
repeat
  if (Fewer than 6 tool rounds?) then (yes)
    :Bind the four tools;
  else (round cap)
    :Invoke model without tools;
  endif
  :Ollama gets system rules, retrieved guidance,
  chat history and tool results;
  :Stream model chunks and tool_call events;
  if (Model requests tools?) then (yes)
    if (Private-data tool?) then (yes)
      :get_accounts / get_debts / get_spending;
      :Gateway reads user-scoped DB rows;
      :Allowlist + scrub + pseudonymize;
      :Audit the minimized context locally;
    else (public guidance)
      :search_kb -> local embeddings + Chroma;
    endif
    :Tool result returns to agent;
    :Stream tool_result events; increment round count;
  endif
repeat while (Model requested tools?) is (yes) not (no)
:Send done (or error); checkpoints saved during graph;
:Finish and release user lock;
stop
note right
The app displays retrieved source URLs.
Retrieval is not proof each claim is supported.

Gateway audit covers financial context,
not the complete conversation prompt.
User messages go to the local model directly.
end note
@enduml
